<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sudan refers both to the modern country on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and, historically, to the bilad al-Sudan, the broad belt of West and Central African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">savannah</a> south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. Arab geographers used the term for the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu</a> empires. The term appears in many profiles, including those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sudan.jpg" alt="Sudan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sudan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
